    "quote": "For any algorithm, any $B > 0$, any $T \\geq 1$ and any $\\theta \\in \\mathcal{E}_{A}(B) = \\left\\{ \\theta \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d+2}, \\|\\theta \\|_{A} = B\\right\\}$ there exists a bandit problem with mean-rewards vector $\\theta' \\in \\mathcal{E}_{A}(B)$ in a neighbourhood of $\\theta$ such that $\\|\\theta - \\theta'\\|^2_A \\le \\min (\\sigma dB /\\sqrt{T} , 4 B^2)$ and : $R_T(\\theta') \\ge \\min ( \\frac{ \\sigma d \\sqrt{T}}{16} , \\frac{B T}{4})$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Locally asymptotically minimax lower bound with Gaussian noise; Assouad construction. Dimension of the space is d+2."
  },
